+- Exactly-once: one database transaction locks the queue row (`FOR UPDATE`),
+  picks the ordered candidate, then locks the candidate row (`FOR UPDATE`)
+  and re-checks it is still `waiting` before marking it `called` with
+  `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id`. A lost race skips to the next
+  candidate. Only the write-once-allowed fields (`status`, `called_at`,
+  `called_by_user_id`) change, so the `Ticket` model `updating` guard holds.
 
